Violations reported in the log files
------------------------------------

The CAPTURE VIOLATIONS that are reported in the scaninsert synthesis runs can
be ignored. These violations are reported due to the clock gating effect of the
OR logic on MPMCCLK to generate the MPMC output clocks MPMCCLKOUT[3:0].

An example of such violations is in the file
 log/Mpmc_scaninsert_vhdl_vhdl_synth.log on line no.s 424 and 6861.

Warnings reported in the log files
----------------------------------

Synopsys produces the following warning when the fanout of any net exceeds
1000. 
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Warning: Design %s contains %d high-fanout nets. A fanout number of 
1000 will be used for delay calculations involving these nets. (TIM-134)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This warning appears in the current Mpmc logs and reports. It has been checked
that this warning is being issued only for clocks and resets, and that there
are no buffers present on Clocks and Resets.
